{
 "id": "P23",
 "kind": "echarts",
 "title": "Every monitor scores the same 1,000 programs, recorded once",
 "section": "setup",
 "order": 10,
 "caption": "Each of 500 APPS coding problems comes with a clean, human-written solution and a backdoored one written by an older AI model. A monitor reads each program with its comments removed and gives it a suspicion score. We swept the settings in the bottom row.",
 "notes": [
  "The code is fixed: we never ask a model to write new backdoors in the main runs, so every monitor and every setting is judged on identical inputs and only the monitor calls cost money.",
  "A backdoor passes the problem's tests but prints a wrong answer on one secret input the attacker knows. The dataset only keeps backdoors that were checked to work."
 ],
